PROMPT: INTERNET / ELECTRONIC BANKING - STRUCTURED INFORMATION EXTRACTION

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OBJECTIVE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Extract structured information from Board Resolution (BR) and Minutes of Meeting (MoM) documents related to internet and electronic banking, authorized persons, and signing instructions with 100% accuracy and zero hallucination.

Output must strictly follow the JSON structure defined at the end of this prompt.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS - READ CAREFULLY
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. SCOPE & SOURCE VALIDATION
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- ONLY extract information from the Board Resolution or Minutes of Meeting sections (including their Annexes or Schedules).
- NEVER infer, assume, or generate information not explicitly stated in the document.
- If information is absent or unclear, return "N/A".
- Do NOT create placeholder data or fictional entries.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. PRODUCT TYPE IDENTIFICATION
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Identify the product type by detecting keywords in the document.

For now only one product type is supported:
"Internet / Electronic Banking" - identified by the presence of any of the following keywords:
 - appointed System Administrators, make changes to the online banking profile, subscribe for electronic banking
 - electronic banking services, internet banking services, electronic banking, electronic platforms
 - E-banking, HSBCnet, H2H, API's, channels

If these keywords are found, set:
 "product_type": "Internet / Electronic Banking"

If none of these keywords are found, do not extract any information and return:
 {"Accounts": []}

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. PRODUCT CATEGORY IDENTIFICATION (AP ONLY)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
For Internet / Electronic Banking, only the AP (Authorised Person) category is applicable. 

A person is identified as AP if the document describes them as having general authority to represent the customer, open accounts, sign terms, and make mandate changes.
Keywords identifying AP powers:
 - Subscribe for electronic banking channels or platforms
 - Authorise third parties to manage the Channels
 - Appoint administrators and manage authorisation levels, delegate authority
 - signs contracts, legally possible to resolve again, delegate, acting on behalf, represent, negotiate, draft and sign documents, appoint/revoke, open and manage, close.

Rule:
 - Always set "product_category": "AP" for all extracted entries in this section.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. ACCOUNT NUMBER EXTRACTION RULES (STRICT SEPARATION)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- CRITICAL INHERITANCE: Look for global or general "Signatory Lists", "Annexes", or "Schedules" located elsewhere in the document that list the company's account numbers. 
- Extract specific account numbers that follow standard banking account number formats (e.g., 21345060, 21345052, 7891-2345-6789) from these global lists.
- STRICT NO-CLUBBING RULE: NEVER comma-separate or combine multiple account numbers into a single entry. Every individual account number must have its own distinct and separate object in the output "Accounts" array, even if the authorised persons and signing rules are 100% identical.
- If the document applies electronic banking rules to specific accounts listed elsewhere in the document (e.g., "in connection with the Account(s)"), extract and link those specific account numbers to the Electronic Banking output, creating one object per account.
- IF the document explicitly mentions "All Accounts" or "All Bank Accounts" in relation to internet banking, extract and output exactly "All Accounts".
- If absolutely no specific account number or "All Accounts" is mentioned anywhere in the document, set "Account Number": "N/A".

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. SUB-PRODUCT IDENTIFICATION & POPULATION RULES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SCANNING RULE — SEARCH THE ENTIRE DOCUMENT:
Scan every individual clause, sub-clause, and bullet point across the entire document. 
When a section contains a numbered or lettered list (e.g., clauses a, b, c...), 
YOU MUST evaluate EACH lettered/numbered item SEPARATELY and independently. 
NEVER reject an entire list block because some items are general banking powers. 
Each item must pass or fail on its own merits.

A clause is ONLY extracted as a Sub-Product if it passes BOTH gates:

GATE 1 — The clause itself must explicitly contain at least one of these terms:
  • internet banking / internet banking facilities
  • electronic banking / electronic banking facilities
  • electronic banking platforms / electronic platforms
  • electronic banking systems / connectivity channels
  • System Administrator(s)
  • online banking profile
  • E-banking / HSBCnet / H2H / API's
  • Channels / E-Channels (in a digital context)
  • authorisation levels (on a digital platform)
  • user access (in context of banking platforms)
  • login PIN / token administration

  CRITICAL: Evaluate Gate 1 on the text of that individual clause only — 
  not on the heading or surrounding clauses.

GATE 2 — Ask: "Would this power exist even without internet/electronic banking?"
  If YES → REJECT (e.g., general account opening, signing checks, revoking mandates).
  If NO  → ACCEPT (e.g., reset of login PIN, assigning digital user access, platform admin).

Step 1 — Link qualifying sub-products to each Account Number from Section 4. Duplicate the sub-products for each individual account object if they apply to multiple accounts.
Step 2 — Each qualifying sub-product gets its own object in the "Sub-Products" array with its own "Signing Rule" array.
If no clauses pass both gates, set "Sub-Products": []

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. LIST OF AUTHORISED PERSON (AP)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Field Name: "List of Authorised Person"

CRITICAL INHERITANCE: You MUST extract the comprehensive list of personnel from the document's main "Signatory List" or Annex. DO NOT limit this list to only the specific individuals named in the Electronic Banking section.

Fields to extract per person:
 | Field | Description |
 |-------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
 | Name | Full human name. CRITICAL: If the document only lists generic roles/titles (e.g., "Director 1", "Designee") and NO specific human name is provided, you MUST set "Name" to "N/A" and extract the role into the "Designation" field. |
 | Action | Normalized action - see Action Rules below |
 | ID Number | Government ID if present, otherwise 'N/A' |
 | Designation | Position/Role/Title (e.g., CFO, Director, Treasury). You MUST search the surrounding context in the document for this. NEVER use structural headings (like "Officer Signatories" or "Group A") as a Designation. If a specific title is not mentioned for a person, return "N/A". |
 | Group | Group designation or category. If names are listed under a common structural heading or title in an Annex/Exhibit (e.g., "Officer Signatories", "Local Signatories", "Group A"), extract that overarching heading as the Group. |
 | Specific Effective Date | Date in DD-MMM-YYYY format - see Effective Date Rules |

ACTION NORMALIZATION RULES:
 Only include a person if an explicit action word is present. Normalize as follows:

 'appoint' / 'add' / 'accede' -> "add"
 'revoke' / 'terminate' / 'dismiss' / 'withdraw' / 'cancel' / 'remove' / 'removed' / 'resign' / 'delete' -> "delete"

 *** NEW - REPLACE ACTION ***
 'replace' / 'substitute' / 'amend' / 'update' / 'modify' 
 / 'supersede' (when referring to a specific person being replaced) 
 / any other synonym of replacement EXCEPT the word 'supersede' used in a whole-document context -> "replace"
 *** END NEW ***

 *** NEW - SUPERSEDE ACTION ***
 'supersede' - ONLY when used in the context that the ENTIRE document or resolution supersedes all previous resolutions or appointments (e.g., "all previous resolutions are hereby superseded by this document", "this resolution supersedes all prior board resolutions").

 When this whole-document supersede context is detected:
 -> Set Action = "supersede" for ALL persons in the list, overriding any earlier action (add / amend / replace) that was assigned to them earlier in the document.
 -> "supersede" as an action takes the highest priority and overrides all other actions when the whole-document supersede context is present.
 *** END NEW ***

 If NO action is explicitly stated for a name -> "N/A"

 NEVER infer any action from context alone - it must be explicitly stated.

ACTION ORDERING RULE:
 Within each list, order entries as:
 1. All "add" actions first
 2. All "delete" actions second
 3. All "replace" actions third
 4. All "supersede" actions fourth
 5. All "N/A" actions last

SPECIFIC EFFECTIVE DATE RULES:
 - Scan the document's header, preamble, or title for board meeting dates or resolution passing dates (e.g., "Meeting held on 27th September 2025"). If found, apply this as the global effective date for ALL persons (e.g., "27-SEP-2025").
 - If a specific effective date is mentioned for an individual person -> populate only for that person.
 - If no effective date is mentioned anywhere in the document or header -> 'N/A' for all
 - Always convert to DD-MMM-YYYY format (e.g., 27-SEP-2025)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. SIGNING RULE EXTRACTION
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fields:
 "Signing Limit" - exact text outlining constraints, limits, or amounts (e.g., "In accordance with signatory list...", "up to HKD 500,000")
 if left blank or marked with a dash ("-") -> use "N/A"

 "Signing Rule" - exact signing pattern or authorized persons assigned to the power.
 CRITICAL: If a global resolution dictates how signatories must act (e.g., "acting jointly with one (1) other Officer Signatory..."), capture this exact phrasing as the Signing Rule for the Sub-Products. If specific individuals or roles (e.g., "Director 1, Director 2, or Designee") are named next to a sub-product, capture them exactly.

Rules:
 - Capture exact limits and persons - never round, infer, or modify.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8. PROCESSING WORKFLOW - FOLLOW THIS ORDER
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1. Detect product type using keywords -> if not found return {"Accounts": []}
 2. Scan document headers for meeting dates to set the global Specific Effective Date.
 3. Scan the document for whole-document supersede context to determine if a global "supersede" action applies.
 4. Scan the entire document (including Annexes) for global Account Numbers.
 5. Create ONE distinct JSON object in the "Accounts" array for EACH individual Account Number found.
 6. Scan the entire document (including Annexes) for the overarching Signatory List. Populate the "List of Authorised Person" within EACH account object. Map overarching structural headings (like "Officer Signatories") to the Group field. Search the surrounding text for specific Designations (use "N/A" if none found). Apply global "supersede" action ONLY IF a trigger word was found in step 3.
 7. Scan every individual clause against the GATE 1 and GATE 2 filtering rules. ONLY extract qualifying electronic/digital banking sub-products. Reject general banking clauses.
 8. Extract Signing Limits and Signing Rules per Sub-Product and apply them to EACH account object.
 9. Validate against Quality Assurance Checklist below.

